{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-10978" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/09482b1e9903bff25b16b2239975831e6d54440a8f8ea78f5739b0eafee3d9e8.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y=-2{x}^{2}-x+3$, the $x$-axis and the $y$-axis, shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-10978" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-2{x}^{2}-x+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-1{\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x+3{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{1}-1\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{1}+3x{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-2(\\frac{1}{3}-0)-1(\\frac{1}{2}-0)+3(1-0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}+3 \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-10978" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dbdad623d43671805a1cf25e54c1bfbc603831b9e5635a2c304f874410921eeb"} {"question" "q-10978" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-10978" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{19}{6}"] ["math" "-\\frac{27}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{11}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{17}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{19}{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-10978" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{11}{6}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-345319" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/0a4b4be4f7de918b847245372077e159f60f3834bb37ef00f4873e63b4cea894.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y={e}^{x}$ and the $x$-axis between $x=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)$ and $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)$, as shown above. Find the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-345319" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{x}{|}_{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)} \\\\  & =2-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-345319" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dbdad623d43671805a1cf25e54c1bfbc603831b9e5635a2c304f874410921eeb"} {"question" "q-345319" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-345319" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-345322" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/66bf8c1144de1ad65938345d2937fddd6fb43ec4822a2b98a9b5383ca2609567.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=-2{x}^{2}+3$ and the $x$-axis between $x=0$ and $x=1$, as shown above. Find the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-345322" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-2{x}^{2}+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+3x){|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{2}{3}+3)-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-345322" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dbdad623d43671805a1cf25e54c1bfbc603831b9e5635a2c304f874410921eeb"} {"question" "q-345322" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-345322" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-54474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/de15e1e9433a3560cbc8268904f4f62fbbb721c3b5b9a700c59fea0941829406.png)\n\nThe area of the shaded region between the curve $y={x}^{3}+8$ and the $x$-axis is given by the integral expression below. What is the value of $a?$\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{a}^{2}({x}^{3}+8)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-54474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To get $a$, we need to find the $x$-intercepts of the curve $y={x}^{3}+8.$ \n\nWe solve the equation for $y=0$: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}+8 & =y \\\\ {x}^{3}+8 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{3} & =-8 \\\\ x & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-54474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dbdad623d43671805a1cf25e54c1bfbc603831b9e5635a2c304f874410921eeb"} {"question" "q-54474" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-54474" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "-2\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "-\\sqrt[3]{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-54474" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-316022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/b5432ed129d85a3718f8e5ebe0cca141731c366d1b32e8e72d0916c60c34de2c.png)\n\nA region in the $x$-$y$ plane is bounded by the curve $y={sec}^{2}⁡x+\\frac{1}{x}$, and the $x$-axis between $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$, as shown above. \nFind the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-316022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}({sec}^{2}⁡(x)+\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{sec}^{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)){|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{3})-(\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi /3}{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-316022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dbdad623d43671805a1cf25e54c1bfbc603831b9e5635a2c304f874410921eeb"} {"question" "q-316022" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-316022" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{3}+\\ln(2)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-73333" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/1819bad0219f1709a01100daad00beb25a8bbc3688f9fe7c41be53bad8010455.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}$, the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=-0.5$ and $x=0.5$, as shown above. What is the area of the region?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-73333" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-0.5}^{0.5}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-0.5}^{0.5}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x{|}_{-0.5}^{0.5} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0.5)-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-0.5)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+(-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-73333" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dbdad623d43671805a1cf25e54c1bfbc603831b9e5635a2c304f874410921eeb"} {"question" "q-73333" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-73333" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-73333" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi }{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-103824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/97cf633bce7a8eeef443757e62d52f356c911b6aee3d8019d434d514416b0049.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and the $x$-axis between $x=-\\pi $ and $x=0$, as shown above. What is the area of the region?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-103824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{|}_{-\\pi }^{0} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)-(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\pi )) \\\\  & =-1-(1) \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-103824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dbdad623d43671805a1cf25e54c1bfbc603831b9e5635a2c304f874410921eeb"} {"question" "q-103824" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-103824" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\pi "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-103824" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-345381" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/dce89dbea62566c0ee897bffe0638458970799bafdc7d7c8e5084328fef38bef.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}$, the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=-1$ and $x=1$, as shown above. Find the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-345381" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-arcsin\\,(\\frac{x}{2}){|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =-(arcsin\\,(\\frac{1}{2})-arcsin\\,(-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+(-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is \n\n$$\nA=-{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-345381" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dbdad623d43671805a1cf25e54c1bfbc603831b9e5635a2c304f874410921eeb"} {"question" "q-345381" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-345381" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-345343" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/34eb73b6bd93f9a45b666ed0599719a09b54948d1d81b14ceea9b46f99b75054.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y=-{x}^{2}-1$, the $x$-axis, and the line $x=-1$ and $x=1$ (shown above). Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-345343" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(-{x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{-1}^{1}-x{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =-(\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{(-1)^{3}}{3})-(1-(-1)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}-2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is \n\n$$\nA=-{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{8}{3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-345343" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dbdad623d43671805a1cf25e54c1bfbc603831b9e5635a2c304f874410921eeb"} {"question" "q-345343" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-345343" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{8}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-316024" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/d282e4afd0a66dd79fecf474da9f618a5970197943044d24208f86c4c43781e6.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}$, the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ and $x=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$, as shown above. Find the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-316024" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x{|}_{-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{\\sqrt{2}/2} \\\\  & =-(arcsin\\,(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})-arcsin\\,(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+(-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is \n\n$$\nA=-{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-316024" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dbdad623d43671805a1cf25e54c1bfbc603831b9e5635a2c304f874410921eeb"} {"question" "q-316024" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "q-316024" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb3d95d350e4957278088d324a69bbb0cd6e85b73d7a8e654f0c3af28ced00d4"} {"question" "e-781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the area between the curve $y=x^2-2x+2,$ the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=0$ and $x=2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/6b85f10cde49017eac1c56ad1b8abbcdf3033a367d5e1eb162dd89fbb6141461.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/example-781.json" "file_sha256" "c9a9c600744b415fd48bc7ef3b773aca59f4e42bd56ff68e9f6dd91f9fb8cab0"} {"question" "e-781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}-2x+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-2{\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x+2{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{2}-2\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{2}+2x{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{8}{3}-0)-2(2-0)+2(2-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}-4+4 \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/example-781.json" "file_sha256" "c9a9c600744b415fd48bc7ef3b773aca59f4e42bd56ff68e9f6dd91f9fb8cab0"} {"question" "e-782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the area of the closed region between the curve $y=x^2-1$ and the $x$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/example-782.json" "file_sha256" "276ce04d087c93e79aa2a23f6efa7f9ec928dfe9351aa289342eb9e566f444ce"} {"question" "e-782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the intersections of the curve with the $x$-axis:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-1 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1 \\\\ x & =\\pm 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe draw a sketch of the region, as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/9b78aad41f84f6a6997914bd8d4243f30cb0ebea4edb5305962dc11c7a46a807.png)\n\nWe want the area between the curve $y=x^2-1$ and the $x$-axis, from $x=-1$ to $x=1.$ To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}({x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{-1}^{1}-x{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{3}-(-\\frac{1}{3}))-(1-(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}-2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $\\dfrac{4}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/example-782.json" "file_sha256" "276ce04d087c93e79aa2a23f6efa7f9ec928dfe9351aa289342eb9e566f444ce"}] "usage" {"e-781" [] "e-782" []} "basis" 1101 "retractions" [[17592186096502 :question/problem "Find the area between the curve $y=x^2-2x+2$, the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=0$ and $x=2$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1040/Source/Images/cd089b9532fe77a9dea0d813bf425efc.png)"] [17592186096502 :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= ∫_{a}^{b}y(x)dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}(x^{2} - 2x + 2)dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}x^{2}dx - 2∫_{0}^{2}xdx + 2∫_{0}^{2}dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{x^{3}}{3}\\begin{vmatrix}_{0}^{2} - 2 \\cdot \\frac{x^{2}}{2} & _{0}^{2} + 2x\\end{vmatrix}_{0}^{2} \\\\\n&= (\\frac{8}{3} - 0) - 2(2 - 0) + 2(2 - 0) \\\\\n&= \\frac{8}{3} - 4 + 4 \\\\\n&= \\frac{8}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186096503 :question/worked-solution "First, we find the intersections of the curve with the $x$-axis:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{2} - 1 &= 0 \\\\\nx^{2} &= 1 \\\\\nx &= ± 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe draw a sketch of the region, as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1040/Source/Images/92bd9521485f93f43b1f96172bd73ba5.png)\n\nWe want the area between the curve $y=x^2-1$ and the $x$-axis, from $x=-1$ to $x=1$. To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= ∫_{a}^{b}y(x)dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{-1}^{1}(x^{2} - 1)dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{-1}^{1}x^{2}dx - ∫_{-1}^{1}dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{x^{3}}{3} \\mid _{-1}^{1} - x \\mid _{-1}^{1} \\\\\n&= (\\frac{1}{3} - (-\\frac{1}{3})) - (1 - (-1)) \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{3} - 2 \\\\\n&=-\\frac{4}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4}{3}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
